                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
                    %br/
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D6+N%3D%282%2C0%29+SCFT"} D=6 N=(2,0) SCFT
                    %br/
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D6+N%3D%281%2C0%29+SCFT"} D=6 N=(1,0) SCFT
            %p
              (
              %a{:href => "supersymmetry#Shnider88"}> Shnider 88
              , also
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "supersymmetry#Nahm78"} Nahm 78
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "supersymmetry#Minwalla98"} Minwalla 98, section 4.2
          %p
            …with
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (2,0)
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/self-dual+higher+gauge+theory"} self-dual higher gauge theory
            whose field configurations are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connections+on+a+2-bundle"} connections on a 2-bundle
            (a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundle+with+connection"} circle 2-bundle with connection
            in the abelian case).
          %p
            This was derived by
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#ClausKalloshProeyen97"} Claus, Kallosh &amp; van Proeyen 1997
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+sigma-model"} Green-Schwarz sigma-model
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
            around the embedding in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/asymptotic+boundary"} asymptotic boundary
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS-spacetime"} AdS-spacetime
            that is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/near-horizon+geometry"} near-horizon geometry
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+brane"} black
            M5-brane.
          %p
            In accord with this the
            %a{:href => "AdS-CFT#AdS7CFT6"} AdS7-CFT6
            correspondence predicts that the nonabelian 6d theory is the corresponding theory for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            coincident M5-branes.
          %p
            In the non-abelian case it is expected (
            %a{:href => "#Witten07"}> Witten 07
            ) that the compactification of such theories are at the heart of the phenomenon that leads to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S-duality"} S-duality
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Yang-Mills+theory"} super Yang-Mills theory
            and further to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+Langlands+duality"} geometric Langlands duality
            (
            %a{:href => "#Witten09"}> Witten 09
            ).
          %p
            Due to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/self-dual+higher+gauge+theory"} self-duality
            a characterization of these theories by an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
            is subtle. Therefore more direct descriptions are still under investigation (for instance
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#SSW11"} SSW11
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Moore11"} Moore11
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Moore12"} Moore 12
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#GeometricEngineering Geometric engineering
          %p
            For
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+engineering"} geometric engineering
            of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/6d+%282%2C0%29-superconformal+QFT"} 6d (2,0)-superconformal QFT
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "duality+between+M-theory+on+Z2-orbifolds+and+type+IIB+string+theory+on+K3-fibrations#GeometricEngineeringOfThe6d2SuperconformalQFT"} duality between M-theory on Z2-orbifolds and type IIB string theory on K3-fibrations – Geometric engineering of 6d (2,0)-SCFT
          %h3#holographic_dual Holographic dual
          %p
            Under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS-CFT"} AdS7/CFT6
            the 6d
            = succeed "-superconformal" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (2,0)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11-dimensional+supergravity"} M-theory
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti+de+Sitter+spacetime"} anti de Sitter spacetime
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi AdS
                      %mn 7
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 4
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} AdS_7 \times S^4
          %p
            See
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FCFT+correspondence"} AdS/CFT correspondence
            for more on this.
          %h3#realization_of_quantum_chromodynamics Realization of quantum chromodynamics
          %p
            See at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS-QCD+correspondence"} AdS-QCD correspondence
          %h3#solitonic_1branes Solitonic 1-branes
          %p
            The 5d
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (2,0)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SCFT"} SCFT
            has tensionless 1-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane"} brane
            configurations. From the point of view of the ambient
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11-dimensional+supergravity"} 11-dimensional supergravity
            these are the boundaries of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-branes"} M2-branes
            ending on the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-branes"} M5-branes
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#GGT"} GGT
          %h3#CompactificationOnARiemannSurface Compactification on a Riemann surface and AGT correspondence
          .float_right_image{:style => "margin: 0px 20px 10px 20px"}
            %img{:alt => "Compactification diagram", :src => "/nlab/files/6d_qft_graph.gif", :width => "600px"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              (graphics taken from (
              %a{:href => "#Workshop14"}> Workshop 14
              ))
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kaluza-Klein+mechanism"} compactification
            of the 5-brane on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+surface"} Riemann surface
            yields as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theory+%28physics%29"} theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/N%3D2+D%3D4+super+Yang-Mills+theory"} N=2 D=4 super Yang-Mills theory
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "N%3D2+D%3D4+super+Yang-Mills+theory#ConstructionByCompactificationOf5Branes"} N=2 D=4 SYM – Construction by compactification of 5-branes
          %p
            The
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AGT+correspondence"} AGT correspondence
            relates the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partition+function"} partition function
            of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SU
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 3
                        %mi g
                        %mo −
                        %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(2)^{n+3g-3}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/N%3D2+D%3D4+super+Yang-Mills+theory"} N=2 D=4 super Yang-Mills theory
            obtained by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kaluza-Klein+mechanism"} compactifying
            the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 6
                  %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 6d
            M5-brane theory on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+surface"} Riemann surface
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mo ,
                      %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{g,n}
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/genus"} genus
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            punctures to 2d
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Liouville+theory"} Liouville theory
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %mo ,
                        %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{g,n}
          %p
            More generally, this kind of construction allows to describe the 6d (2,0)-theory as a “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+SCFT"} 2d SCFT
            with values in
            = succeed "\u201D." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Yang-Mills+theory"} 4d SYM
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AGT+correspondence"} AGT correspondence
            for more on this.
          %h3#twistor_space_description Twistor space description
          %p
            Famously the solutions to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/self-dual+Yang-Mills+theory"} self-dual Yang-Mills theory
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            4 can be obtained as images of degree-2 cohomology classes under the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Penrose-Ward+twistor+transform"} Penrose-Ward twistor transform
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
            contains a 2-form
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/self-dual+higher+gauge+field"} self-dual higher gauge field
            it seems natural to expect that it can be described by a higher analogy of the twistor transform. For references exploring this idea see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "twistor+space#ReferencesApplicationToSelfDual2FormField"} twistor space – References – Application to the self-dual 2-form field in 6d
          %h2#related_entries Related entries
          %ul
